AB  - The property and casualty (P&C) insurance cloud-native transformation has hastened the use of continuous delivery and microservices architecture that makes release governance and operational risk management more complex. The conventional rule-based governance systems are not usually flexible to meet the dynamic regulatory needs, rollout risks and scalability of the system in a large scale. This research suggests a smart risk-conscious release governance framework based on agentic artificial intelligence to improve cloud-native P&C insurance system decision-making. The framework uses independent AI agents to determine deployment risks, implement regulatory regulations and mirror out release approvals at CI/CD pipelines. Experimental studies and simulation are performed to compare the proposed method with the traditional rule-based models of governance. The outcomes indicate a positive shift in the release failure rate, the mean time to recovery, the compliance adherence, and the deployment velocity. The ability of the agentic AI approach to withstand regulatory alterations, the occurrence of calamity, and infrastructure collapse through stress testing further confirms the power and strength of the approach. The results suggest that agentic AI allows scalable, explainable, and adaptive release governance to facilitate operational flexibility and regulatory confidence in innovative insurance platforms.
ER  - 

