AB  - The rapid growth of enterprise software ecosystems presents new challenges to quality at scale. Traditional Quality Assurance (QA) methods thatare based on manual verification and static automation tools have difficulty catching up with the speed of continuous delivery pipelines and system integrations. We propose AI-Augmented Quality Assurance (AI-QA): a framework which combines predictive analytics, generative AI and intelligent automation to improve quality, speed and reliability in an enterprise context. The proposed framework uses machine learning models to predict defective modules, utilizes large language models (LLMs) to automatically produce and improve a set of test cases, and implements feedback-driven self-learning loops to provide continuous improvement. Empirical results in a real-world enterprise setting show up to 40% % reduction in validation effort and 30% increase in defect detection efficiency, along with significant improvements in terms of regression coverage. This study describes the architecture, implementation, and performance evaluation of this AI-QA framework and what its implications are for future DevOps pipelines and digital transformation efforts.
ER  - 

