AB  - Modern financial software systems rely heavily on continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipelines to deploy features, security updates, and infrastructure changes at high velocity. While DevSecOps practices have improved automation in software delivery, most pipeline governance still depends on manual decision-making for handling failures, vulnerabilities, and deployment anomalies. This human dependency introduces operational delays, increases security risk exposure, and limits scalability of software delivery pipelines. This paper proposes a GenAI-driven autonomous DevSecOps orchestration framework designed to enable predictive security analytics and automated control actions in CI/CD pipelines. The framework integrates real-time pipeline telemetry with machine learning models capable of detecting anomalies, forecasting deployment failures, and identifying security risks prior to pipeline completion. A GenAI reasoning layer orchestrates remediation strategies including automated rollbacks, security gating, and adaptive pipeline optimization. Experimental evaluation using representative CI/CD telemetry demonstrates that the proposed system improves failure prediction accuracy, reduces mean time to recovery, and enhances overall deployment reliability in financial software infrastructure. The results indicate that integrating generative AI with DevSecOps orchestration can significantly enhance resilience and security in modern financial technology platforms.
ER  - 

