AB  - Infrastructure automation entails automating physical and virtual infrastructure management and operation through software. This encompasses software deployment, confer management, and monitoring. The Future of Infrastructure Automation with Cloud Computing: Introduction Cloud computing is changing how we do business. Cloud computing has many benefits, the most striking being flexible and scalable infrastructure. Organizations can automatically allocate or deal locates compute resources as required without manual interference. This allows automation tools to automate routine tasks as well as operations. Infrastructure management has changed with the arrival of Infrastructure as Code; treats infrastructure configuration as code, it enables this infrastructure as code, which allows for more reliable and consistent deployment and configuration of your infrastructure with less room for human error. DevOps practices have facilitated the automation of several practices from the software development cycle to achieve continuous delivery. As part of its continued evolution, AI and machine learning are increasingly integrated into infrastructure automation tools, giving rise to predictive maintenance and self-healing capabilities. In turn, this minimizes downtime and enhances system performance.
ER  - 

